  "ambiguities": [
    {
      "paragraph": "(j)",
      "description": "\"Within 9,450 cycles after the effective date\" does not say whose cycles (the engine's or the drum's).",
      "readings": [
        "Engine flight cycles after the effective date (used here).",
        "The drum's cycles after the effective date."
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "(j)",
      "description": "Paragraph (j) is headed \"Mandatory Terminating Action\" but does not list which paragraphs it ends.",
      "readings": [
        "It ends the inspections of (e), (f), and (h) (used here, once its compliance time has passed).",
        "It ends only the repetitive inspections of (f)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "(e)",
      "description": "\"Within 200 cycles of the drum accumulating 6,250 cycles\" is read as the drum reaching 6,450 cycles since new; likewise 8,000, 3,750, 12,500, and 9,000 plus 200.",
      "readings": [
        "The drum's cycles since new plus 200 (used here)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "(f)(1)",
      "description": "The repetitive interval depends on the engine's compliance group (A, B, C, E, F: 750 cycles; D: 500), which is in the unavailable bulletin.",
      "readings": [
        "Group unknown: review."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Paragraphs (e)(1) to (e)(5) are printed as subheadings, which the frozen section index does not split, so the initial inspections cite (e) and name the subparagraph in their description.",
    "V2500-A1 engines are in (c)(1) but outside the supported V2500-A5/D5/E5 scope.",
    "Engine compliance groups are in IAE Alert NMSB V2500-ENG-72-A0615 Revision 6, not available, so the initial and repetitive USIs go to review; the terminating action (j) is fully stated and, once its compliance time has passed, decides the engine's status."
  ]
